[{"text":"FieldDerivative[f[x], x, li1, li2, ...] is the derivative of f[x] with respect to space-time variables x and with Lorentz indices li1, li2, ..., where li1, li2, ... have head LorentzIndex.","anchor":"fieldderivative"},{"text":"FieldDerivative[f[x], x, li1, li2, ...] can be given as FieldDerivative[f[x], x, {l1, l2, ...}], where l1 is \\(li1\\) without the head.","anchor":"fieldderivative"},{"text":"FieldDerivative is defined only for objects with head QuantumField. If the space-time derivative of other objects is wanted, the corresponding rule must be specified.","anchor":"fieldderivative"},{"text":"Overview, FCPartialD, ExpandPartialD.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"QuantumField[A, {\\[Mu]}][x] . QuantumField[B, {\\[Nu]}][y] . QuantumField[C, {\\[Rho]}][x] . QuantumField[D, {\\[Sigma]}][y]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[A_{\\mu }(x).B_{\\nu }(y).C_{\\rho }(x).D_{\\sigma }(y)\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FieldDerivative[%, x, {\\[Mu]}] // DotExpand","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[A_{\\mu }(x).B_{\\nu }(y).\\left(\\left.(\\partial _{\\mu }C_{\\rho }\\right)\\right)(x).D_{\\sigma }(y)+\\left(\\left.(\\partial _{\\mu }A_{\\mu }\\right)\\right)(x).B_{\\nu }(y).C_{\\rho }(x).D_{\\sigma }(y)\\]","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FieldDerivative[%%, y, {\\[Nu]}] // DotExpand","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[A_{\\mu }(x).B_{\\nu }(y).C_{\\rho }(x).\\left(\\left.(\\partial _{\\nu }D_{\\sigma }\\right)\\right)(y)+A_{\\mu }(x).\\left(\\left.(\\partial _{\\nu }B_{\\nu }\\right)\\right)(y).C_{\\rho }(x).D_{\\sigma }(y)\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"}]